<p><b>🔄 How to update pyTMBot</b></p>

<p>These steps apply if you run pyTMBot with Docker Compose and the service is named <code>pytmbot</code>. If your path or service name is different, adjust the commands below.</p>

<p><b>Recommended steps</b></p>
<ol>
<li>Open the directory with your <code>compose.yaml</code></li>
<li>Pull the latest image</li>
<li>Recreate the service</li>
<li>Check status and recent logs</li>
</ol>

<pre><code class="language-bash">cd /opt/pytmbot
docker compose pull pytmbot
docker compose up -d --force-recreate pytmbot
docker compose ps
docker compose logs -n 50 pytmbot</code></pre>

<p><b>Optional cleanup</b></p>
<pre><code class="language-bash">docker image prune -f</code></pre>

<p>ℹ️ <i>Your mounted config and secret files stay in place.</i></p>
